  "verbalization": "Hydrocortisone is proposed to interact with SN12K1 through a multi-step mechanism involving the enzyme 2,3-dichloro-1-propanol dehalogenase. This enzyme is targeted by Hydrocortisone, and its activity is further modulated by Pyridoxine phosphate, which acts as a cofactor in the enzymatic process. The presence of SN12K1 as a downstream target of both the dehalogenase and Pyridoxine phosphate suggests a potential regulatory pathway where Hydrocortisone influences the activity of the dehalogenase, which in turn affects the function of Pyridoxine phosphate. This interconnected network of targets implies that Hydrocortisone may exert its effects on SN12K1 through the modulation of enzymatic activity, potentially altering metabolic pathways or cellular processes governed by SN12K1. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Hydrocortisone and SN12K1, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
